{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaCKLeadingBiasCorrectionIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaCKLeadingBiasCorrectionIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.bias_correction_recovers_alg_exact_when_truncated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.bias_correction_recovers_alg_exact_when_truncated","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity.lean#L79-L90","doc":"**Bias correction is EXACT when the ladder terminates.**\n\nIf the algebraic ladder is zero from index `k+2` onward (a\ntruncated generating function), the bias correction exactly\nrecovers `c_alg k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.bias_correction_residual_is_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.bias_correction_residual_is_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity.lean#L67-L77","doc":"**The residual after bias correction is exactly `-c_alg (k+2) · u²`.**\n\nRestating the previous result by isolating the residual on the RHS.\nShows that the leading bias correction is exact up to a single\nquadratic-in-u term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.bias_correction_recovers_alg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.bias_correction_recovers_alg","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity.lean#L52-L65","doc":"**Bias correction recovers c_alg modulo u².**\n\nGiven the leading-order bias model, the bias-corrected value\n`ĉ_k - ĉ_{k+1} * u` equals `c_alg k - c_alg (k+2) * u²`.  The\nresidual is structurally at order `u²` and bounded by the\n(k+2)-th algebraic coefficient.\n\nPure ring identity, holds over any commutative ring. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity","label":"prop:q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.biasedExtraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CkLeadingBiasCorrection.biasedExtraction","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-c-k-leading-bias-correction-identity.lean#L40-L50","doc":"The leading-order extraction-bias model for the joint-fit c_k\nextraction.  Given algebraic ladder coefficients `c_alg` and a\nsmall parameter `u`, the extracted ĉ_j is modeled as\n\n    ĉ_j = c_alg j + c_alg (j+1) * u.\n\nThis is the structural assumption motivating the bias-correction\nidentity below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}